{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\X2Mail\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "route-unreferenced",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "POST /index.php/apps/x2mail/  x2mail.page.indexpost  appinfo/routes.php:3 routes",
        "GET /index.php/apps/x2mail/app/  x2mail.page.appget  appinfo/routes.php:3 routes",
        "POST /index.php/apps/x2mail/app/  x2mail.page.apppost  appinfo/routes.php:3 routes"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "Nothing in the app calls 3 routes outside OCS. Looked for: a route name or a path in the PHP source and the templates, in 1 file of the frontend source and in the navigation of info.xml. A route stays behind when the frontend stops calling it. A route that only a client outside the app calls shows here as well, unless its method allows requests from other origins (CORS).",
        "  POST /index.php/apps/x2mail/  x2mail.page.indexpost  appinfo/routes.php:3 routes",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/x2mail/app/  x2mail.page.appget  appinfo/routes.php:3 routes",
        "  POST /index.php/apps/x2mail/app/  x2mail.page.apppost  appinfo/routes.php:3 routes"
      ]
    },
